<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <!--
    ros2_control hardware description for a big_yam arm + linear_4310 gripper
    on a single CAN bus, driven by i2rt_hardware_interface/YamSystemInterface.

    motor_id/motor_type/kp/kd values below are the real hardware defaults for
    ArmType.BIG_YAM + GripperType.LINEAR_4310, taken directly from
    i2rt/robots/config/{big_yam.yml,linear_4310.yml} in the Python driver.
    Note this arm differs meaningfully from the standard "yam" (see
    yam_ros2_control.xacro): joints 1-2 are DM6248 (not DM4340). Do not reuse
    yam_ros2_control.xacro's values for this arm or vice versa.

    direction values are NOT taken as-is from big_yam.yml's `directions`
    array — that array was calibrated against the Python driver's MuJoCo
    model (i2rt/robot_models/arm/big_yam/big_yam.xml), which has joint4's
    local axis flipped (`axis="0 0 -1"`, every other joint is "0 0 1") and a
    different accumulated mounting-frame orientation feeding into joint6.
    Verified numerically (chained rotation matrices from both the MuJoCo
    body/joint tree and this URDF's joint origins, applied to the local
    z-axis at the zero-configuration pose): joints 1,2,3,5 agree between the
    two models and use big_yam.yml's directions unchanged; joints 4 and 6
    disagree in sign and are negated here relative to big_yam.yml's raw
    values (which are +1 for both). Confirmed against real hardware: RViz
    showed joint4/6 rotating opposite the real arm before this fix.

    gravity_comp_factor per joint is big_yam.yml's `gravity_comp_factor`
    array — a per-joint scale on the KDL-computed gravity feed-forward torque
    that YamSystemInterface adds every write() cycle (mirrors
    MotorChainRobot.update()'s `g * gravity_comp_factor` in the Python
    reference). kp/kd are still the URDF-fixed position-hold gains used
    whenever a controller doesn't claim the (also new) kp/kd command
    interfaces — see YamSystemInterface's class comment for the isfinite
    fallback logic. gravity_root_link/gravity_tip_link/max_gravity_torque_nm
    configure the KDL chain used for that gravity computation.

    The gripper's mimic joint (gripper_mimic_joint, see gripper_linear_4310.xacro)
    intentionally has no entry here: it's a passive <mimic> follower with no
    motor of its own, so robot_state_publisher computes its transform from
    gripper_joint's published state without needing one.

    gripper_joint (motor 7) DOES have an entry below: motor_id/motor_type/kp/kd
    are linear_4310.yml's real hardware defaults (DM4310, kp=20.0, kd=0.5).
    direction/offset are fixed at 1.0/0.0 (not tuned per-arm like the other
    joints) because YamSystemInterface applies its own calibration-derived
    raw<->URDF-units mapping for this joint on top of raw feedback, and that
    requires DmChain's own offset/direction transform to stay a no-op here,
    see requires_calibration below and yam_system_interface.hpp's
    GripperCalibration comment. gravity_comp_factor is fixed at 0.0: the
    gravity KDL chain (base_link->link_6) doesn't include this joint (it
    branches off link_6, not part of that chain), so the value is inert, but
    set explicitly rather than left at the (also-inert-here) 1.0 default.

    requires_calibration=true makes YamSystemInterface probe this joint's
    hard stops every on_activate() (real hardware only; mock hardware uses
    a different plugin entirely and ignores all of this): it drives the
    gripper into both hard stops with calibration_test_torque_nm of torque
    for up to calibration_max_duration_s per direction, and maps the raw
    motor range it detects onto [calibration_lower_limit_m,
    calibration_upper_limit_m] (gripper_linear_4310.xacro's <limit> tag,
    duplicated here since the hardware component doesn't read the URDF's own
    <joint><limit>). Keep the gripper clear of obstructions before activating
    real hardware. See yam_system_interface.cpp's run_gripper_calibrations().

    use_mock_hardware:=true swaps in ros2_control's built-in
    mock_components/GenericSystem instead of the real CAN-backed plugin — no
    can_channel, no hardware, joints just mirror their last command back as
    state. Use this for MoveIt/RViz/IK checks with no arm connected at all.
    (GenericSystem has no impedance/MIT control model at all, so it ignores
    compliant_mode/compliant_kp/compliant_kd below entirely - they only
    affect real hardware.)

    compliant_mode:=true makes every joint's kp/kd fall back to
    compliant_kp/compliant_kd (instead of that joint's own stiff "kp"/"kd"
    <param> below) whenever nothing has claimed the kp/kd command interfaces
    - i.e. a hand-backdrivable default: YamSystemInterface's gravity feed-
    forward (see its class comment) is unconditional and unaffected either
    way, so with compliant_kp at its default of 0.0 that feed-forward
    becomes the only torque holding the arm up against gravity, and
    compliant_kd supplies a small viscous damping term (against zero
    velocity) so it doesn't feel like free-floating/oscillating when
    hand-moved. compliant_kp defaults to 0.0 (pure gravity-comp, no drift
    correction at all) rather than some nonzero starting value, so turning
    compliant_mode on never changes behavior on hardware you haven't
    explicitly tuned compliant_kp for yet - see YamSystemInterface's class
    comment for what a nonzero value buys you (gentle anti-drift correction
    that still doesn't fight hand-guidance) and why it's safe to raise
    incrementally rather than something picked once and left alone.
    Intended for a teleoperation leader arm meant to be hand-guided, not
    commanded - see i2rt_teleop's leader_follower.launch.py, which sets
    compliant_mode true for the leader and leaves it false (this arm's
    normal stiff position-hold behavior) for the follower. Explicit kp/kd
    commands from an actual controller always take priority over this
    fallback regardless.
  -->
  <xacro:macro name="big_yam_ros2_control"
    params="prefix can_channel:=can0 use_mock_hardware:=false compliant_mode:=false compliant_kp:=0.0 compliant_kd:=0.3">

    <ros2_control name="${prefix}big_yam_system" type="system">
      <hardware>
        <xacro:if value="${use_mock_hardware}">
          <plugin>mock_components/GenericSystem</plugin>
        </xacro:if>
        <xacro:unless value="${use_mock_hardware}">
          <plugin>i2rt_hardware_interface/YamSystemInterface</plugin>
          <param name="can_channel">${can_channel}</param>
          <param name="gravity_root_link">${prefix}base_link</param>
          <param name="gravity_tip_link">${prefix}link_6</param>
          <param name="max_gravity_torque_nm">25.0</param>
          <!-- xacro coerces a "true"/"false" arg into a Python bool, which
               would render as capitalized "True"/"False" text if
               interpolated directly - force it back to the lowercase
               literal YamSystemInterface's on_init actually compares
               against. -->
          <param name="compliant_mode">${'true' if compliant_mode else 'false'}</param>
          <param name="compliant_kp">${compliant_kp}</param>
          <param name="compliant_kd">${compliant_kd}</param>
        </xacro:unless>
      </hardware>

      <joint name="${prefix}joint1">
        <param name="motor_id">1</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM6248</param>
        <param name="direction">-1</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="kp">80.0</param>
        <param name="kd">5.0</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">1.0</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

      <joint name="${prefix}joint2">
        <param name="motor_id">2</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM6248</param>
        <param name="direction">-1</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="kp">80.0</param>
        <param name="kd">5.0</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">1.1</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

      <joint name="${prefix}joint3">
        <param name="motor_id">3</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM4340</param>
        <param name="direction">1</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="kp">80.0</param>
        <param name="kd">5.0</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">1.0</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

      <joint name="${prefix}joint4">
        <param name="motor_id">4</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM4340</param>
        <param name="direction">-1</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="kp">40.0</param>
        <param name="kd">3.0</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">1.1</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

      <joint name="${prefix}joint5">
        <param name="motor_id">5</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM4310</param>
        <param name="direction">-1</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="kp">40.0</param>
        <param name="kd">1.5</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">1.0</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

      <joint name="${prefix}joint6">
        <param name="motor_id">6</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM4310</param>
        <param name="direction">-1</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="kp">10.0</param>
        <param name="kd">1.5</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">1.0</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

      <joint name="${prefix}gripper_joint">
        <param name="motor_id">7</param>
        <param name="motor_type">DM4310</param>
        <param name="kp">20.0</param>
        <param name="kd">0.5</param>
        <param name="direction">1.0</param>
        <param name="offset">0.0</param>
        <param name="gravity_comp_factor">0.0</param>
        <param name="requires_calibration">true</param>
        <!-- Verified against real hardware: the default polarity (1.0) paired
             the raw hard-stops backwards; closed read back as open. -1.0
             matches this gripper's actual motor wiring/rotation sense. -->
        <param name="calibration_polarity">-1.0</param>
        <param name="calibration_lower_limit_m">-0.0475</param>
        <param name="calibration_upper_limit_m">0.0</param>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <command_interface name="velocity"/>
        <command_interface name="effort"/>
        <command_interface name="kp"/>
        <command_interface name="kd"/>
        <state_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
        <state_interface name="effort"/>
      </joint>

    </ros2_control>

  </xacro:macro>

</robot>
